    "description": "Dyson just made a toothbrush with a camera inside. 🪥\n\nThe Dyson CameraJet takes 28 images a second of your teeth. On-device AI spots the gaps between them, and within 100 milliseconds fires a jet of mouthwash right in, so you brush and floss at the same time. The app can even show a live feed of your mouth. The catch: regular toothpaste foams up and blocks the camera, so you need a non-foaming one. Price: $499.\n\nWould you pay that to skip flossing? 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
